  <h2>About Rebecca</h2>
  <p>
    Rebecca Keller holds a Master's in Performance Science from the <strong>Royal College of Music in London</strong>. As Director of <strong>Ear to Brain Fitness<sup class="tm">&trade;</sup></strong>, she designs rhythm- and music-based programs that support auditory processing across the lifespan — translating cutting-edge research on neural timing into hands-on training patients can practice every day.
  </p>
  <p>
    Her work bridges music, neuroscience, and clinical audiology, making complex brain science accessible to patients of every age.
  </p>

  <h2>Role at Duet</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Designs Ear to Brain Fitness<sup class="tm">&trade;</sup> programs</li>
    <li>Rhythm- and music-based neural training</li>
    <li>Auditory processing support across the lifespan</li>
    <li>Patient education and program coaching</li>
